{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791628055,"nonce":"/NCwu0q7EU2dsuT3pgskelbq9gU=","title":"Re-tier sites recompute the function's CFG, loops and liveness once per header","message":"retier_state_for (crates/ash/src/cranelift/air.rs) built a CfgInfo and LoopForest in retier_worth_polling and a CfgInfo plus Liveness in Layout::new for every header of the function, on every Cranelift compile, with the global RETIER lock held for the Layout part. A function with several leaf loops paid the dataflow several times.\n\nIt showed once OSR eligibility became per loop (7ad3b41): more functions get re-tier sites, and in --mode jit, which compiles every reached function at first call, Cranelift compile time for test_stdlib went up. NUC, ASH_PROFILE=phases, pinned, 10 runs each, median cranelift compile ms: base 91.6, with the wider eligibility 102.8 (+12%), after computing the CFG, forest and liveness once per function 88.5 (-3%).\n\nLayout::with_liveness takes the liveness; osr::analyze_loops takes the CFG and forest.","files":null}]}